		<Property name="Table" value="TkLocalisationEntry" _id="UI_S23_LEAVE_PLANET_LOG">
			<Property name="Id" value="UI_S23_LEAVE_PLANET_LOG" />
			<Property name="English" value="&lt;STELLAR&gt;No Man's Sky&lt;&gt; was an idea that maybe everyone who plays games has thought about at some point. What if you could explore the universe? What if a game world didn't have boundaries? It's certainly something we had always wanted to see exist...&#xA;&#xA;For us there was a technical excitement. No one had done seamless travel between planets, or used procedural generation to make 3D planets - but it should be possible? And wouldn't it be fun to try?&#xA;&#xA;There was also an emotional motivation. We wanted to really have that feeling of exploration in a game, true exploration where no one knows what's over the hill. That science fiction fantasy of landing on a planet for the first time.&#xA;&#xA;So sat in our little office one night, we started to build it. There was never really a plan, we had no idea how wild a journey it would become, but it felt exciting." />
