		<Property name="Table" value="TkLocalisationEntry" _id="UI_S23_ECHOES_LOG">
			<Property name="Id" value="UI_S23_ECHOES_LOG" />
			<Property name="English" value="Interceptor, the Singularity expedition (where players helped Specialist Polo construct a robot) and now finally the &lt;STELLAR&gt;Echoes&lt;&gt; update were all designed as a sort of breadcrumb trail to introduce a new alien race we had been working on: the robotic Autophage. &#xA;&#xA;Narratively, these Korvax-derived lifeforms have always inhabited the universe, so we came up with a &quot;scan to reveal&quot; mechanic to unveil them to Travellers. We also introduced the &quot;modular customisation&quot; system in Echoes, allowing players to construct their own staff Multi-Tool. That system proved to be very versatile. The same underlying code enabled modular ship construction in Orbital, and fossil assembly in Relics.&#xA;&#xA;Echoes also brought in Dreadnought freighter battles, with a trench run gameplay loop inspired by a favourite scene in one of our favourite sci-fi franchises. We love that No Man's Sky can support this action side of sci-fi as well as more reflective exploration." />
