			<Property name="English" value="&lt;STELLAR&gt;Orbital&lt;&gt;, &lt;STELLAR&gt;Omega&lt;&gt; and the &lt;STELLAR&gt;Adrift&lt;&gt; expedition all released in fairly quick succession in early 2024! &#xA;&#xA;&lt;STELLAR&gt;Omega&lt;&gt; was an especially challenging update. We essentially built a demo in the form of a free expedition, which has different technical requirements on different platforms, and which also had to serve as a sort of tutorial for new players. We also allowed players to start expeditions from existing saves - something the community had been requesting for a while - which required some delicate data-masking and context-handling of save games. We always feel extremely cautious around anything related to save data. Many of our players have thousands of hours of progress by now.&#xA;&#xA;&lt;STELLAR&gt;Orbital&lt;&gt; introduced two massive features we'd been working on for a while: a complete redesign of space stations, and constructable starships.&#xA;&#xA;Some players have been wanting to customise ships forever, but ship-hunting is such a core part of No Man's Sky that we couldn't simply remove that feature. Instead, we implemented the ability to collect modules and construct new ships from scratch, while acknowledging naturally-occurring ships with an &quot;authenticated&quot; badge.&#xA;&#xA;We decided not to redesign the abandoned versions of space stations. It feels somehow fitting that they are a relic of the old design..." />
