			<Property name="English" value="When we split Worlds into two updates, we had intended to release &lt;STELLAR&gt;Worlds Part II&lt;&gt; shortly afterwards. The player response to Part I was so positive that we thought actually, we want to listen to feedback and spend longer perfecting Part II. Of course, that meant it grew even bigger!&#xA;&#xA;We added a bunch of new biomes and creatures, as well as even more improvements to water rendering. We made &quot;abandoned mode&quot;, an idea first introduced in Adrift, into a complete game mode. Perhaps most significantly, we added entirely new star systems - something we hadn't done since launch - which gave the narrative team a really exciting opportunity for building a new story. It gave us the freedom to add new terrain shapes and waterworlds. Finally we could add gas giants, something we had dreamt of since launch.&#xA;&#xA;In the background we are also working on an ambitious new game, Light No Fire. Some key tech developed for this was now being sent back - almost from the future - for No Man's Sky, allowing us to keep expanding the universe." />
