		<Property name="Table" value="TkLocalisationEntry" _id="UI_S23_REMNANT_LOG">
			<Property name="Id" value="UI_S23_REMNANT_LOG" />
			<Property name="English" value="After the physics tech we'd developed for Voyagers, we were hungry to add more physical elements to the gameplay of No Man's Sky. &lt;STELLAR&gt;Remnant&lt;&gt; was originally conceived with the plan to use multiple physics worlds for loading cargo into your exocraft - the same technology that allows players to stand inside a Corvette and not get jettisoned into space when it moves. &#xA;&#xA;We tried that... it was ok... but we struck upon something much more fun. Introducing a gravity gun we embraced the chaos of physics and allowed the cargo to jiggle and bounce with the movement of the Colossus - and sometimes have precious cargo fall out. As we saw at launch, there were some great moments during development of precious cargo rolling down hill at the last moment." />
